              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ānser, ānseris — \"a goose\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ānser is inherited, usually traced to Proto-Indo-European ghh2ens, \"goose\" (EtymDB 2.1); Latin lost the first sound. Greek khēn, \"goose\", and English goose and gander are cousins (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
